Fillets: an analytic blend's contact running along a concave edge of its
face is off that face there (mitcad#343).

A pocket's ceiling rounded with a wall (radius 8) up to a block at the
rounding's end whose side lies exactly where the rounding touches the
ceiling: past the end the ceiling's contact line runs along the block's
concave edge with the ceiling. SplitKPart hatches the line on the ceiling;
the hatcher took that part as inside the ceiling or outside it as the line
lay a rounding error (1e-14) to one side of the edge or the other. On one
side of a stored design the line's domain ended at the block, the corner
cut the blend with the face at the end and the result was the bodies
stored in the file; on the mirrored side it ran on past the block to the
ceiling's rim (21.6 further), the end's contact did not reach the face at
the end, and the corner failed or built faces of reversed orientation.

No ball of the blend touches the face along a concave edge of it (the
face beyond rises into the ball), so HatchOffConcaveEdges hatches such a
line moved off the face across those edges, by the shift HatchOnBoundary
uses, and its ends found near a vertex are snapped to the vertex as
HatchOnBoundary's are. Straight lines only; without such an edge nothing
changes.

Upstream: new.
